  "scope": "The actually inspected Design English migration, its current 21 accepted contract bindings, the shared migration/checker implementation, and the recorded manifest/guide/CI configuration snapshots. Plan task-binding migration and final GitHub CI/merge outcomes are not yet reviewed or accepted by this report.",
  "observations": [
    "New migration records use new directories; original accepted wrappers/reviews are not rewritten by the migration implementation.",
    "create_records compares every required input byte with the specified Git source commit and builds dependency snapshots in topological order.",
    "Preparation and acceptance are separate, and original.accept requires a verdict from the same recorded independent reviewer over the exact evidence/review manifest hashes.",
    "The new per-file coverage verifier checks reviewer != translation_author; actual author assignments in the not-yet-created manifest remain to be examined.",
    "The proposed narrow JSON projection removes only hash/source/review binding metadata, retaining all content, versions, IDs, statuses, authorization, dependencies and paths. Removed metadata must pass the independent acceptance gate.",
    "The complete manifest path/author lists and immutable-original classifications were read. They exactly partition the baseline CJK inventories: Design 64 translated + 16 immutable; Plan 140 translated + 6 immutable. No pre-existing non-English file is omitted.",
    "The explicit R31 normalization maps only compare three technical paths to compare 3 technical paths in the numeric checker for research-tasks/R31.md. The complete source sentence states the quantity 3; the translated sentence states the same quantity as three. The source/target file hashes and independent review remain mandatory, and a changed quantity four was independently rejected.",
    "The Design workflow checks out the actual PR head/push SHA with full history and read-only contents permissions, then runs strict verification without --preflight. The existing Plan workflow retains every old command and adds four strict translation/provenance/completion gates. No native experiment execution was introduced.",
    "The final Design acceptance index was reread after root applied acceptance: all 21 contracts are accepted, every previously inspected one of the 63 records is byte-identical, and the original contract reviewer exact attestation matches all 21 evidence/review pairs.",
    "This report does not bind a final complete registry/graph SHA into the corresponding review cycle. Their full bytes are in the translation manifest; semantic projections and independent actual binding attestations serve their separate roles."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "EN-MIG-P01",
      "severity": "must_fix_for_complete_provenance_verification",
      "status": "resolved_after_author_fix_and_independent_readback",
      "issue": "New translation_provenance/prior_accepted_evidence/prior_accepted_reviews/index prior_acceptance fields are written during preparation but the inherited verification and acceptance paths do not compare those values with the fixed historical accepted baseline.",
      "requested_fix": "Validate exact prior subjects, index and wrapper/evidence identities against baseline on prepare, verify and accept.",
      "resolution": "Read the added provenance checks in prepare/verify/accept and the standalone Design verifier. Independently compared all 21 actual prior subjects, index identities, old evidence/reviews and new wrapper provenance against the fixed accepted baseline; all match."
    },
    {
      "id": "EN-MIG-P02",
      "severity": "resolved_implementation_observation",
      "status": "resolved_after_author_fix_and_independent_readback",
      "issue": "Historical subject author fields alone do not establish translator/reviewer independence.",
      "resolution": "Actual manifests identify the correct translation authors. Every one of the 64 Design and 140 Plan translated entries has an exact accepted review by a different actual executor, including the narrow JSON projection cases. This remains a scoped executor review, not GitHub-account identity authentication."
    },
    {
      "id": "EN-MIG-P03",
      "severity": "must_fix_for_claimed_code_preservation",
      "status": "resolved_after_author_fix_and_independent_readback",
      "issue": "binding_text_paths bypasses all inline-code comparison rather than only the migrated current contract SHA literals.",
      "requested_fix": "Normalize only the declared SHA-256 hash literals, then compare every inline-code token normally.",
      "resolution": "Only labelled SHA-256 literals are normalized before all inline-code token comparison. A changed SafeHandle token was correctly rejected despite an allowed migrated hash."
    },
    {
      "id": "EN-MIG-P04",
      "severity": "must_fix_for_valid_translation_acceptance",
      "status": "resolved_after_author_fix_and_independent_readback",
      "issue": "Translated SQL -- comments are rejected by a //-only stripping rule. Unconditional // stripping can also erase executable string content such as URLs.",
      "requested_fix": "Allow the actual C#/Rust // and SQL -- comment translations with unchanged executable prefix/content, without stripping comment markers from string literals.",
      "resolution": "Conservative comment rules preserve executable prefixes and disallow quoted prefixes for inline comments. Legitimate SQL/C#/Rust comment translations pass; the demonstrated comment marker inside a C# string literal now fails."
    },
    {
      "id": "EN-MIG-P05",
      "severity": "minor_documentation_accuracy",
      "status": "resolved_after_author_fix_and_independent_readback",
      "issue": "The new Design guide initially located reviewer-authored binding attestations with the generated verification records.",
      "resolution": "The guide now correctly distinguishes verification/english-translation/ snapshots/evidence/wrappers from docs/traceability/reviews/english-translation/ reviewer attestations; the actual contract-bindings.json path was inspected."
    }
